docs/design/dao.stream.md-75-  outcome as data; the reader decides what missing data means.
docs/design/dao.stream.md-76-- All expected operational outcomes are data, not exceptions or callbacks.
docs/design/dao.stream.md-77-- No operation waits. Every operation returns what is true at the moment it is
docs/design/dao.stream.md-78-  called; an answer not yet knowable arrives later as data.
docs/design/dao.stream.md:79:- No hidden global state. DaoStream keeps no registry of streams, handles, or
docs/design/dao.stream.md-80-  observers, and no operation consults ambient state.
docs/design/dao.stream.md-81-- A logical stream has an identity that is plain data, the same through every
docs/design/dao.stream.md:82:  handle on it, stable across attachment lifecycles and across serialization.
docs/design/dao.stream.md-83-  Projecting that identity never fails.
