docs/design/dao.stream.md-201-  descriptor via `descriptor`, whose outcome set is `{ok}` with
docs/design/dao.stream.md-202-  `:dao.stream/descriptor` — identity is universal and outlives any
docs/design/dao.stream.md:203:  attachment, so `descriptor` has no failure outcome.
docs/design/dao.stream.md-204-- `attach!` consumes a portable descriptor and returns a handle on an
docs/design/dao.stream.md:205:  attachment to the **same** logical stream the descriptor names. Attaching
docs/design/dao.stream.md-206-  never creates.
docs/design/dao.stream.md-207-- A creation specification says how to build a stream. A descriptor only
docs/design/dao.stream.md-208-  names one — never executable code, never a construction program, never a
docs/design/dao.stream.md-209-  request to load a plugin.
