docs/design/dao.stream.md-415-A transport also declares **which outcomes it produces**, and for each one it
docs/design/dao.stream.md-416-excludes, why. There are three honest reasons: the outcome's precondition is
docs/design/dao.stream.md:417:impossible by the transport's nature (an unbounded log never evicts, so never
docs/design/dao.stream.md:418:reports `gap`); another policy answers the same condition, named (a ring buffer
docs/design/dao.stream.md:419:evicts rather than refusing, so pressure surfaces as a reported `gap` and never
docs/design/dao.stream.md-420-as `full`); or the answer is displaced to another channel, named (a transport
docs/design/dao.stream.md-421-that cannot know a remote answer at call time reports it as data elsewhere). An
docs/design/dao.stream.md-422-exclusion with no stated reason is an unimplemented outcome, not a declaration.
